4. Noah-MP v5.0 (UCAR) -- withheld; not in this distribution
==========================================================================

MPAS-Model v8.4.2 carries NCAR's community Noah-MP land surface model,
version 5.0, in physics_noahmp/, under UCAR's Noah-MP terms
(physics_noahmp/LICENSE.txt, sha256
bd58c64131e08711ea7eb436f7a9520187626e6dcd0550fd6947f3060697d212; the
RRFSx fork carries the same file). Those terms say:

    You shall not sell, license or transfer for a fee the Software, or any
    work that in any manner contains the Software.

Apache-2.0 grants the right to sell, so the public distribution of
gpuwm-hex does not carry the CUDA port of Noah-MP v5.0
(src/hexcore/mpasphys/noahmp_v842.py, and urban_v842.py, which composes
with it) or the tests and oracles that transcribe it (tests/noahmp_v842/,
tests/urban_v842/). The list of withheld paths is tools/licence_holds.json
(hold ucar-noahmp-v5). A private build that keeps the port also keeps
UCAR's terms in full (licenses/LICENSE-Noah-MP-UCAR.txt) and the notices
those terms require (licenses/NOTICE-Noah-MP-UCAR-private-builds.txt); in
such a build UCAR's terms, not Apache-2.0, govern that portion.

No default runs Noah-MP v5.0: the MPAS suites default to Noah (section 3).
An MPAS suite run with config_lsm_scheme='sf_noahmp' is refused unless it
names the terms with --licence-opt-in ucar-noahmp. With the opt-in, the
native-cpu backend runs Noah-MP from a native library the user builds with
the same opt-in (gpuwm-hex physics-resources build --licence-opt-in
ucar-noahmp, which compiles Noah-MP v5.0 from upstream on the user's
machine), and the hex-cuda backend is refused in a distribution that does
not carry the port. By default that command builds the library with an
Apache-2.0 interface stub in place of Noah-MP v5.0.

The Noah-MP that gpuwm-hex runs by default is a different code: the ArWen
suite's WRF-lineage Noah-MP v4.x, which gpuwm ports from WRF v4.6.1's
Noah-MP (NCAR/noahmp commit 848f54ad3d28c4303151fe5ad83724e232694422, the
submodule WRF v4.6.1 pins). That commit carries no licence file, and WRF
distributes it under the WRF public-domain notice (section 3 and gpuwm's
NOTICE). Noah-MP's v5.0 release notes describe v5.0 as a refactoring
"without physics changes", but the v4.x code is not bitwise with MPAS's
v5.0 and gpuwm-hex does not claim that it is.

